From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Oct 2023 10:52:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0141/1695] drivers: clk: add clock PM callback in
 clk-stm32mp15.c

Implement PM for stm32mp15 clocks. The platform considers 2 types
of low power transitions, STOP and SUSPEND. STOP low power mode
is when CPU context is always preserved but from SoC domains
may need to be resumed. SUSPEND transitions are suspend requests
where CPU context may or may not be preserved upon the selected
deepest state platform is allowed to reach.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git fbc99617480625984e1d2b9b22498d7f678bf251 drivers: clk: add clock PM callback in clk-stm32mp15.c]
Signed-off-by: Etienne Carriere <etienne.carriere@st.com>
Change-Id: Ia598705bbd5350a090b5f3ecb243d4f186d9c0e8
